113.89394 123.558271 \nL 116.837462 132.435226 \nL 119.780983 140.596924 \nL 122.724505 148.100994 \nL 125.668027 155.000427 \nL 128.611549 161.343939 \nL 131.555071 167.176325 \nL 134.498592 172.538768 \nL 137.442114 177.469134 \nL 140.385636 182.002237 \nL 143.329158 186.170087 \nL 146.693183 190.523738 \nL 150.057208 194.478843 \nL 153.421232 198.071887 \nL 156.785257 201.336015 \nL 160.149282 204.301335 \nL 163.513307 206.995202 \nL 167.297835 209.732181 \nL 171.082363 212.188948 \nL 174.866891 214.394192 \nL 179.071922 216.580696 \nL 183.276954 218.519933 \nL 187.902488 220.400777 \nL 192.528022 222.049022 \nL 197.574059 223.615531 \nL 203.0406 225.076399 \nL 208.927644 226.414549 \nL 215.23519 227.619503 \nL 222.383743 228.74697 \nL 229.952799 229.714823 \nL 238.783365 230.60901 \nL 247.61393 231.303999 \nL 247.61393 231.303999 \n\" style=\"fill:none;stroke:#000000;stroke-linecap:square;stroke-width:2.3;\"></path>\n   </g>\n  </g>\n </g>\n <defs>\n  <clipPath id=\"pccc14b8bd6\">\n   <rect height=\"260.82\" width=\"268.898496\" x=\"7.2\" y=\"7.2\"></rect>\n  </clipPath>\n </defs>\n</svg>\n<div role=\"region\" aria-label=\"Long description for graph of a curve\" class=\"sr-only\"><ul><li>Moving from left to right:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>The curve passes from quadrant 2 to quadrant 1.</li>\n<li>In quadrant 2, the curve trends down sharply to the point (0 comma 3).</li>\n<li>In quadrant 1, the curve trends down gradually.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>As x increases, the curve approaches the line y equals 0.</li>\n<li>The curve passes through the following points:<br>\n<ul>\n<li>(0 comma 3)</li>\n<li>approximately (0.5 comma 0.7)</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul></div></figure></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The graph of the exponential function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is shown, where <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>. The <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. What is the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[],"keys":["3"],"correct_answer":["3"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>. It's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph shown is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The graph passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</math> is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1730147357399,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"02c67921","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":2,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1730147357399,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"fc448e0e-6144-425a-a9b3-2ff8ee674f1b","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"da30f8ac-5a33-4748-a817-78a12fb948ec","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"answerOptions":[],"externalid":"fc448e0e-6144-425a-a9b3-2ff8ee674f1b","keys":["3"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The correct answer is <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math>. It's given that the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph shown is <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma y right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. The graph passes through the point <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 0 comma 3 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi>\n</mat