$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_000_3455aa71.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_001_937dbf09.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_002_fb81fbd3.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 15, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_003_1995f714.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 20, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, NULL, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is correct. Since 5 is a factor of both terms, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_005_ec342366.png" alt="5 x"></span> and 15, the given expression can be factored and rewritten as <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_006_3455aa71.png" alt="5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting 5 from the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression. Choice C is incorrect and may result from factoring 5 from only the first term, not both terms, of the given expression. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding 5 to the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>
$SATQ$, false, 7, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$Multiple Choice$SATQ$, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ${"questionId":"0354c7de","external_id":null,"disclosed_item_id":"027693-DC","source":"disclosed","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":1,"type":"mcq","stimulus":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_004_13a48247.png\" alt=\"5 x plus 15\"></span></span></p></div>\n","stem":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is equivalent to the given expression?</p>\n","answerOptions":[{"id":"a","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_000_3455aa71.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"b","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_001_937dbf09.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"c","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_002_fb81fbd3.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 15, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},{"id":"d","content":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_003_1995f714.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 20, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"}],"keys":null,"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Since 5 is a factor of both terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_005_ec342366.png\" alt=\"5 x\"></span> and 15, the given expression can be factored and rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0354c7de/img_006_3455aa71.png\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting 5 from the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression. Choice C is incorrect and may result from factoring 5 from only the first term, not both terms, of the given expression. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding 5 to the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n","answer_style":"Multiple Choice","section":"Math","image_count":7,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959621,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"0354c7de","skill_cd":"P.A.","score_band_range_cd":1,"skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","createDate":1691007959621,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"027693-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"edb21dda-4c91-47ed-9f4f-6b586cec3b11","difficulty":"E"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"027693-DC","section":"Math","body":"<div class=\"stimulus_reference \" xmlns=\"http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/apip/apipv1p0/qtiitem/imsqti_v2p1\"><p class=\"standalone_statement style:1 \"><span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 x plus 15\"></span></span></p></div>\n","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">Which of the following is equivalent to the given expression?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"Multiple Choice","choices":{"a":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},"b":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 10, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},"c":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 15, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"},"d":{"body":"<p class=\"choice_paragraph \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 20, close parenthesis\"></span></p>\n"}},"correct_choice":"a","rationale":"<p>Choice A is correct. Since 5 is a factor of both terms, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 x\"></span> and 15, the given expression can be factored and rewritten as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"5 times, open parenthesis, x plus 3, close parenthesis\"></span>.<p>Choice B is incorrect and may result from subtracting 5 from the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression. Choice C is incorrect and may result from factoring 5 from only the first term, not both terms, of the given expression. Choice D is incorrect and may result from adding 5 to the constant when factoring 5 from the given expression.</p><p>&nbsp;</p></p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959621,"updateDate":1691007959621}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959621, 1691007959621),
    ($SATQ$0380bbdc$SATQ$, $SATQ$2aca4259-cade-40c9-b16c-5635ca1d9ac5$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 4, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">If <math alttext="4 StartRoot 2 x EndRoot equals 16"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>, what is the value of <math alttext="6 x"><mrow>
