	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>16</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext="3"><mn>3</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="6 x equals 48"><mrow>
	<mrow>
		<mn>6</mn>
		<mi>x</mi>
	</mrow>
	<mo>=</mo>
	<mn>48</mn>
</mrow>
</math>. Therefore, the value of <math alttext="6 x"><mrow>
	<mn>6</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math> is <math alttext="48"><mn>48</mn>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="3 x"><mrow>
	<mn>3</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, not <math alttext="6 x"><mrow>
	<mn>6</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="9 x"><mrow>
	<mn>9</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, not <math alttext="6 x"><mrow>
	<mn>6</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This is the value of <math alttext="12 x"><mrow>
	<mn>12</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>, not <math alttext="6 x"><mrow>
	<mn>6</mn>
	<mi>x</mi>
</mrow>
</math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0380bbdc","external_id":"2aca4259-cade-40c9-b16c-5635ca1d9ac5","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"3a09b21e-8b0f-4456-8603-a8c701b2f62a","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables ","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":4,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">If <math alttext=\"4 StartRoot 2 x EndRoot equals 16\"><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>16</mn></mrow></math>, what is the value of <math alttext=\"6 x\"><mrow>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n</mrow>\n</math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"86acde22-0ebd-4ebb-b14d-6589f1506a1d","content":"<p><math alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"0d767fa4-5c95-43a1-91c5-f6820046afd1","content":"<p><math alttext=\"48\"><mn>48</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"967a6e98-3fa6-4bb2-b216-8f7f5a0b9d20","content":"<p><math alttext=\"72\"><mn>72</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce241ab1-b2bb-48f0-8446-104a0aab6dd4","content":"<p><math alttext=\"96\"><mn>96</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["0d767fa4-5c95-43a1-91c5-f6820046afd1"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is correct. Dividing each side of the given equation by <math alttext=\"4\"><mn>4</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"StartRoot 2 x EndRoot equals 4\"><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>. Squaring both sides of this equation yields <math alttext=\"2 x equals 16\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>16</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Multiplying each side of this equation by <math alttext=\"3\"><mn>3</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"6 x equals 48\"><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\