</math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["29"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["29"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="29"><mn>29</mn></math>. The solutions to a quadratic equation in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a x squared plus b x plus c equals 0"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="c"><mi>c</mi></math> are constants, can be calculated using the quadratic formula, which gives two solutions: <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals StartFraction negative b plus StartRoot b squared minus 4 a c EndRoot Over 2 a EndFraction"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>+</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals StartFraction negative b minus StartRoot b squared minus 4 a c EndRoot Over 2 a EndFraction"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><msqrt><msup><mi>b</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>a</mi><mi>c</mi></msqrt></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. The given equation is in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a x squared plus b x plus c equals 0"><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals 1"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals 7">