</math> joules.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"04b985e6","external_id":"f45f8ef3-75e8-4989-991d-8bcf481614f7","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"ccee11b9-1477-4fbf-b932-7236d9e15be5","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The kinetic energy, in joules, of an object with mass <math alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn>\n</math> kilograms traveling at a speed of <math alttext=\"v\"><mi>v</mi>\n</math> meters per second is given by the function <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math>, where&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper K left parenthesis v right parenthesis equals nine halves v squared\"><mi>K</mi><mfenced><mi>v</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>9</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Which of the following is the best interpretation of&nbsp;<math alttext=\"upper K left parenthesis 34 right parenthesis equals 5,202\"><mi>K</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>5,202</mn></mrow></math> in this context?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"653ebe4d-04af-4d72-b997-01d3a16e7f9f","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The object traveling at <math alttext=\"34\"><mn>34</mn>\n</math> meters per second has a kinetic energy of <math alttext=\"5,202\"><mn>5,202</mn>\n</math> joules.</p>"},{"id":"aba92466-330a-4e45-a153-36f7458b82d1","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The object traveling at <math alttext=\"340\"><mn>340</mn>\n</math> meters per second has a kinetic energy of <math alttext=\"5,202\"><mn>5,202</mn>\n</math> joules.</p>"},{"id":"7eb22086-1d2d-4591-9d44-16e552e88f24","content":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The object traveling at <math alttext=\"5,202\"><mn>5,202</mn>\n</math> meters per second 