</math> from both sides of the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="5 x plus 3 equals 0"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields <math alttext="5 x equals negative 3"><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext="5"><mn>5</mn>
</math> yields <math alttext="x equals negative three fifths"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>. Adding <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> to both sides of the equation&nbsp;<math alttext="x minus 8 equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> yields <math alttext="x equals 8"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Therefore, the two solutions to the given equation, <math alttext="5 x squared minus 37 x minus 24 equals 0"><mn>5</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>37</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>24</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, are&nbsp;<math alttext="negative three fifths"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> and <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math>. It follows that <math alttext="8"><mn>8</mn>
</math> is the positive solution to the given equation.</p>
