mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>289</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>. Therefore, <math alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> reaches its minimum when the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> is <math alttext="negative StartFraction 13 Over 2 EndFraction"><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>13</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>. Note that -13/2 and -6.5 are examples of ways to enter a correct answer.</p>
