myrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_007_7fe23461.png" alt="x equals negative 6"></span>. Therefore, there are two solutions to this system of equations, one with an <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate of 6 and the other with an <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_008_c8d23d01.png" alt="negative 6"></span>. Substituting 6 for <span class="italic">x</span> in the second equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_009_14a8d53a.png" alt="y equals, negative 6 times 6, plus 36"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_010_eedaaf46.png" alt="y equals 0"></span>; therefore, one solution is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_011_939951f1.png" alt="the ordered pair 6 comma 0"></span>. Similarly, substituting <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_012_c8d23d01.png" alt="negative 6"></span> for <span class="italic">x</span> in the second equation yields <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_013_c373ed97.png" alt="y equals, negative 6 times negative 6, plus 36"></span>, or <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_014_930c5ad0.png" alt="y equals 72"></span>; therefore, the other solution is <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_015_d73045a5.png" alt="the ordered pair negative 6 comma 72"></span>. It follows then that if <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_016_7284e904.png" alt="the ordered pair x comma y "></span> is a solution to the system, then possible values of <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_017_20edb154.png" alt="x y   "></span> are <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_018_c8504f25.png" alt="6 times 0, equals 0"></span> and <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_019_39c8d0c1.png" alt="negative 6 times 72, equals negative 432"></span>. Only 0 is among the given choices.<p>Choice B is incorrect. This is the <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate of one of the solutions, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_020_939951f1.png" alt="the ordered pair 6 comma 0"></span>. Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or computational errors. Choice D is incorrect. This is the square of the <span class="italic">x</span>-coordinate of one of the solutions, <span class="math-container"><img align="middle" role="math" class="math-img" src="https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/0980fcdd/img_021_939951f1.png" alt="the ordered pair 6 comma 0"></span>.</p></p>
