		<mn>2</mn>
	</msup>
</mrow>
</math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"d17d1f6a-9f1b-4d32-b3ef-1b59e3d78e25","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6\"><mn>6</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"98d7fdda-1e30-4abf-8edc-8e63f8aba501","content":"<p><math alttext=\"7\"><mn>7</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"2917411f-d05f-467b-9545-371067e9655a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"42\"><mn>42</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"d83e9902-a639-4b42-910f-7b25aa9ba4b0","content":"<p><math alttext=\"294\"><mn>294</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["2917411f-d05f-467b-9545-371067e9655a"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. Multiplying both sides of the given equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="42 equals 7 x squared"><mn>42</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the value of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="7 x squared"><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="42"><mn>42</mn></math>.</p>
