    ($SATQ$0a74365c$SATQ$, $SATQ$ff0ab105-aa85-4cb3-a07f-f00a7c55c4e3$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.C.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear functions$SATQ$, $SATQ$M$SATQ$, 5, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The population of the town of Smithville doubled every <math alttext="75"><mn>75</mn>
</math> years from <math alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math> to <math alttext="1959"><mn>1959</mn></math>. The population of this town was <math alttext="240,000"><mn>240,000</mn>
</math> in <math alttext="1959"><mn>1959</mn></math>. What was the population of this town in <math alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math>?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["15000"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["15000"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="15,000"><mn>15,000</mn></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> represent the population of Smithville&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> years after <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math>. Since the population doubled every&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="75"><mn>75</mn></math> years, the relationship between&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> can be represented by an exponential equation in the form <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> is the population of Smithville in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math> and the population increases by a factor of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> every&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> years. It&rsquo;s given that the population doubled, or increased by a factor of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math>, every&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="75"><mn>75</mn></math> years. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b equals 2"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k equals 75"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math>. Substituting&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2"><mn>2</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="b"><mi>b</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="75"><mn>75</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals a left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 75 EndFraction"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>75</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. It's also given that the population of this town was <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000"><mn>240,000</mn></math> in <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1959"><mn>1959</mn></math>. The number of years from&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math> to&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1959"><mn>1959</mn></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1959 minus 1659"><mn>1959</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1659</mn></math>, or&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="300"><mn>300</mn></math> years. Therefore, when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 300"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></math>, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000"><mn>240,000</mn></math>. Substituting&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="300"><mn>300</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000"><mn>240,000</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals a left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 75 EndFraction"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>75</mn></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000 equals a left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction 300 Over 75 EndFraction"><mn>240,000</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mfrac><mn>300</mn><mn>75</mn></mfrac></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000 equals a left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript 4"><mn>240,000</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mn>2</mn></mfenced><mn>4</mn></msup></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="240,000 equals a left parenthesis 16 right parenthesis"><mn>240,000</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="16"><mn>16</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="15,000 equals a"><mn>15,000</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Therefore, the population of this town in&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="1659"><mn>1659</mn></math> was <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="15,000"><mn>15,000</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"0a74365c","external_id":"ff0ab105-aa85-4cb3-a07f-f00a7c55c4e3","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"5e96ce3e-2b8d-4b1e-a4a9-75bc79d8315c","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"M","score_band_range_cd":5,"type":"spr","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The population of the town of Smithville doubled every <math alttext=\"75\"><mn>75</mn>\n</math> years from <math alttext=\"1659\"><mn>1659</mn></math> to <math alttext=\"1959\"><mn>1959</mn></math>. The population of this town was <math alttext=\"240,000\"><mn>240,000</mn>\n</math> in <math alttext=\"1959\"><mn>1959</mn></math>. What was the population of this town in <math alttext=\"1659\"><mn>1659</mn></math>?</p>","answerOptions":null,"keys":["15000"],"correct_answer":["15000"],"rationale":"<p>The correct answer is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"15,000\"><mn>15,000</mn></math>. Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> represent the population of Smithville&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> years after <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1659\"><mn>1659</mn></math>. Since the population doubled every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"75\"><mn>75</mn></math> years, the relationship between&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y\"><mi>y</mi></math> can be represented by an exponential equation in the form <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math>, where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is the population of Smithville in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"1659\"><mn>1659</mn></math> and the population increases by a factor of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> years. It&rsquo;s given that the population doubled, or increased by a factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math>, every&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"75\"><mn>75</mn></math> years. Therefore,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b equals 2\"><mi>b</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 75\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math>. Substituting&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2\"><mn>2</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"b\"><mi>b</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"75\"><mn>75</mn></math> for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math> in the equation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals a left parenthesis b right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over k EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfenced><mi>b</mi></mfenced><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></mfrac></msup></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"y equals a left parenthesis 2 right parenthesis Superscript StartFraction x Over 75 EndFraction\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mfence