thesis plus 29"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mn>0</mn></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>29</mn></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y equals 29"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>29</mn></math>. Therefore, the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 0 comma 29 right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>29</mn><mo>)</mo></math>. It&rsquo;s given that <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="y"><mi>y</mi></math> is the estimated number of scheduled deliveries <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x"><mi>x</mi></math> months after the end of May <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2012"><mn>2012</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 0"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> represents <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="0"><mn>0</mn></math> months after the end of May <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2012"><mn>2012</mn></math>, or the end of May <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2012"><mn>2012</mn></math>. Thus, the best interpretation of the <em>y</em>-intercept of the graph of this equation in the <em>xy</em>-plane is that at the end of May <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="2012"><mn>2012</mn></math>, the estimated number of scheduled deliveries was <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="29"><mn>29</mn></math>.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual errors.</p>
